Rxe7 Rxe7 27. Qc8+ Re8 28. Qc5+ Re7 {Biographical note: Samuel Black MBE FBIM
FRSA (6 January 1915 – 23 January 1999) https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/
Sam_Black_(public_relations) London Boys' Chess Champion; he managed to defeat
the then British champion, William Winter, in 1935 and 1936. During his time
at the University of London, he captained the Chess Club from 1933–4. He was
secretary of Finchley Chess Club and the president of the London North
Circular Chess League until 1997.} 1/2-1/2

