1. e4 c6 2. c4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. cxd5 Qxd5 5. Nc3 Qa5 6. d4 Nf6 7. Nf3 e6 8.
Bd3 Bb4 9. Bd2 O-O 10. Ne5 Nbd7 11. f4 Nd5 12. Qc2 f5 13. O-O Bxc3 14. bxc3 Qd8
15. c4 Nxe5 16. fxe5 Ne7 17. Be3 b6 18. Rad1 Bb7 19. d5 Qd7 20. d6 Rac8 {
?? Aitken} 21. dxe7 Qxe7 22. Qb3 g5 23. c5 Rc6 24. Bb5 Rxc5 25. Rd7 Rxb5 26.
Rxe7 Rxb3 27. axb3 Bd5 28. Bxg5 {n.b. this was a friendly match between
Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire, who at that time did not play in formal
county competitions. It's not important to the game but there seems to be some
confusion as to the extent of Oxfordshire's victory: BCM (April 1935, p177):
"in a recent friendly match Oxfordshire beat Buckinghamshire by 25½ to 24½."
The Times (4 March 1935) gives individual scores and the overall result as
Oxfordshire 13, Buckinghamshire 2. There seems little doubt that the Times has
it right - JS} 1-0

