1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. f3 g6 6. c4 Bg7 7. Nc3 Nc6 8. Be3
O-O 9. Qd2 Nxd4 10. Bxd4 b6 11. O-O-O Ba6 12. h4 Rc8 13. b3 e6 {creates a
weakness but Black must play for ...d5 to free his game} 14. g4 Qe7 15. Qb2 {
"Beginning a combination by which I hoped to win a pawn safely. The game,
however, now becomes very complicated, and I found I had not taken all Black's
resources into account." - Aitken} Rfd8 $1 16. g5 Nh5 17. Bxg7 Nxg7 18. Qa3 Bb7
19. Qxa7 $6 (19. Rh2 $1 a6 $140 20. Rhd2 Ne8 {"Everything is held for the
moment but Black remains very cramped, and has little prospect of freedom."})
19... Qc7 20. Nb5 Qc6 21. Nd4 Qc7 22. Qa3 d5 23. exd5 Bxd5 $1 (23... exd5 24.
Kb1 Qf4 25. Qe7 Ba8 26. Bh3 Rb8 27. c5 $1 bxc5 28. Qxc5 $16) 24. Qb2 Nf5 $1 {
Threat ...Bxc4} 25. Nxf5 $8 gxf5 26. Be2 b5 $5 {An enterprising bid to win} (
26... Bxf3 27. Bxf3 Qf4+ 28. Rd2 Qxf3 29. Rhd1 Qf4 30. Qf6 Rxd2 31. Rxd2 Qxh4 {
and White must take the draw by perpetual check}) 27. Qc3 bxc4 28. bxc4 Rd6 29.
h5 (29. Rd4 e5 30. Rd2 Bxc4) 29... Bxc4 30. Bxc4 Rc6 (30... Qxc4 31. Qxc4 Rxc4+
32. Kb2 Rb6+ (32... Rxd1 {appears to lose}) 33. Ka1 {with some practical
chances in the ending, albeit probably objectively drawish}) 31. Rh4 f4 32. Rd4
e5 33. Re4 Rxc4 34. Rxc4 Qxc4 35. Qxc4 Rxc4+ 36. Kb2 Kg7 37. Rh2 h6 $1 38. Kb3
(38. Rc2 $2 Rd4 39. g6 fxg6 40. Rc7+ Kf6 41. Rc6+ Kf5 42. hxg6 Rd7 $1 $19)
38... Rd4 39. gxh6+ Kxh6 40. Kc3 Ra4 41. Kb3 Rd4 {Source: CHESS, 14 March 1939,
p260 (from Glasgow Herald) (Tim Harding, English Chess Forum, 23 Oct 2020)}
1/2-1/2

