Bxf4 28. fxe4 Nxh4 29. Kf2 Bh5 {In his scorebook, Aitken pencilled the
following note: "This is the best game I played before the outbreak of war,
and the last tournament game for many months. In the interim I had several
casual games at the National Chess Centre, London, and elsewhere." The final
word 'elsewhere' is carefully chosen: had he been more specific, he might have
broken the Official Secrets Act! JS} 0-1

