This was the inaugural National Club Championship: results on other boards 
(Lud-Eagle players first): 2 I Konig ½-½ DV Mardle; 3 H Israel ½-½ ER
Reifenberg; 4 HH Cole 0-1 B Tomlinson; 5 Dr Winterton 0-1 JF Barrett; 6 F
Fischer 1-0 JR Coward. Finished 3-3, Cambridge won on the elimination of
bottom board rule. CHESS, August 1950, p207. Venue was the Anthony Room, Cora
Hotel, Upper Woburn Place (near Euston Station). Play 2.15-7pm, followed by
dinner and presentation of prizes (BCM, August, opp. p245)} 1-0

