Qg5+ 21. Ne3 c5 22. Qd2 {Source: Aitken Book 15. BCM, December 1953, p325:
"Bristol Invitation Tournament.—A second tourney will take place during the
coming months thanks to the continued generosity of a local patron of chess
who has donated £50 as prize money. The competitors are P. Keffler (Bath), M.
E. Poolake (Stroud), F. S. Woolford (Cinderford), D. Mardle and J. Neale 
(Cheltenham), P. Copping (Swindon), C. Sullivan, C. Welch, and A. White 
(Bristol), together with two players of international repute in C. H. O’D.
Alexander and Dr. J. M. Aitken. The games will be played at approximately
fortnightly intervals between now and Easter."} 0-1

