1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. a4
Rb8 9. axb5 axb5 10. Nc3 d6 11. Nd5 Nxd5 12. exd5 Nd4 13. Nxd4 exd4 14. c3 Bf6
15. c4 bxc4 16. Bxc4 Bf5 17. d3 Re8 18. b3 Qd7 19. Rxe8+ Rxe8 20. Bd2 Qe7 21.
Kf1 h6 22. Ra7 Qd7 23. Ba5 Bd8 24. Bb6 Qe7 25. Bb5 Rf8 26. Bxd4 Qh4 27. Ra4
Qxh2 28. Qf3 Qh1+ 29. Ke2 Bg6 30. Ra1 Qh4 31. g4 f5 32. Bd7 Qxg4 33. Qxg4 fxg4
34. Bxg4 Re8+ 35. Kd2 Bf7 36. Bf3 Bg5+ 37. Kc3 Rb8 38. Ra7 Bd8 39. Be4 h5 40.
Ra1 g5 41. Rg1 {Source: Aitken Book 15. BCM, September 1954, p289, has a
lenghty report (though not the score of this game). "Woolverton defended
stoutly against Aitken’s Ruy Lopez on Board 2 and always seemed to be
holding his own. Aitken staged a strong looking demonstration on the Queen’s
side, having possession of the open Queen’s Rook file but at the right
moment Black counter-attacked the sparsely defended King’s wing and White
had to play very accurately indeed to hold on. Eventually the Queens were
forced off and although Black had a passed pawn on the King’s-Rook’s file
it was not possible to prove a win for him." (BCM) Other board scores 
(Cheltenham names first): 1 C H O'D Alexander 1-0 PH Clarke; 3 DV Mardle 1-0
PB Cook; 4 Dr IJ Good 0-1 Dr B Sturgeon; 5 J Ansell 1-0 AJ Morrell; 6 J Neale
1-0 JM Soesan. Cheltenham thus won the 1954 National Club Championship title
by 4½-1½.} 1/2-1/2

